Description: use the Hub distribution identity in Claude-facing pstack guides
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: not-needed

The immutable upstream import describes the upstream cursor-plugins
marketplace as pstack. Our Hub distributes the generated plugin as
pstack-azhouzhou from marketplace pstack-claude. Patch the installed copy
of the upstream README, poteto-help and Claude Code adaptation rather
than writing to the pristine pinned upstream source. The replacement
references the local Hub package directory, not the upstream marketplace.

--- a/pstack/README.md
+++ b/pstack/README.md
@@ -23,9 +23,9 @@
 ```bash
-/plugin marketplace add cursor/plugins
-/plugin install pstack@cursor-plugins
-```
-
-claude code leaves auto-update off for third-party marketplaces, so pstack stays on the version you installed. to turn it on, run `/plugin`, open the **marketplaces** tab, select `cursor-plugins`, and choose **enable auto-update**. to update once by hand, run `claude plugin update pstack@cursor-plugins`.
-
-claude code prefixes plugin commands and agents, so `/poteto-mode` is `/pstack:poteto-mode`. the [claude code adapter](./docs/harness/claude-code.md) maps every other cursor name. in claude code, `/pstack:setup-pstack` writes your model choices to `~/.claude/rules/pstack-models.md`, and a step that needs a cursor-only feature, such as bugbot or automations, is skipped with a one-line note.
+/plugin marketplace add <absolute-Hub-package-directory>
+/plugin install pstack-azhouzhou@pstack-claude
+```
+
+claude code leaves auto-update off for third-party marketplaces, so pstack stays on the version you installed. to turn it on, run `/plugin`, open the **marketplaces** tab, select `pstack-claude`, and choose **enable auto-update**. to update once by hand, run `claude plugin update pstack-azhouzhou@pstack-claude`.
+
+claude code prefixes plugin commands and agents, so `/poteto-mode` is `/pstack-azhouzhou:poteto-mode`. the [claude code adapter](./docs/harness/claude-code.md) maps every other cursor name. in claude code, `/pstack-azhouzhou:setup-pstack` writes your model choices to `~/.claude/rules/pstack-models.md`, and a step that needs a cursor-only feature, such as bugbot or automations, is skipped with a one-line note.

